DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vvmm__ppaaggee__wwiirree() and vvmm__ppaaggee__wwiirree__mmaappppeedd() functions wire the page,
     which prevents it from being reclaimed by the page daemon or when its
     containing object is destroyed.  Both functions require that the page be‐
     long to an object.  The vvmm__ppaaggee__wwiirree__mmaappppeedd() function is for use by the
     pmap(9) layer following a lookup.  This function may fail if mappings of
     the page are concurrently being destroyed, in which case it will return
     false.

     The vvmm__ppaaggee__uunnwwiirree() and vvmm__ppaaggee__uunnwwiirree__nnooqq() functions release a wiring
     of a page.  The vvmm__ppaaggee__uunnwwiirree() function takes a queue index and will
     insert the page into the corresponding page queue upon releasing its last
     wiring.  If the page does not belong to an object and no other references
     to the page exist, vvmm__ppaaggee__uunnwwiirree() will free the page.
     vvmm__ppaaggee__uunnwwiirree__nnooqq() releases the wiring and returns true if it was the
     last wiring of the page.

